---
import ContactCta from '../components/ContactCta.astro';
import Experience from '../components/Experience.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { experience } from '../data/experience';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'About', path: '/about' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Pontus Burman, founder of Papa Bravo"
  description="Pontus Burman is the founder of Papa Bravo. He is Engineering Manager at Avanza, and has led technology, product and transformation at organisations including Getinge, Eniro Group, Unilabs, MedHelp, Trustly and Klarna. Stockholm, Sweden."
  path="/about"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Section narrow>
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Pontus Burman</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Founder of Papa Bravo. I take interim and advisory work in technology, product and
      transformation, and I still build the products the company runs.
    </p>
    <p>
      Based in Stockholm. More than twenty years of this, in companies with very different
      constraints — listed groups, and faster product companies.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Experience" title="What the career has covered">
    <p>
      I am Engineering Manager at Avanza, for two teams, since December 2025. Before that, the
      work includes Program Manager at Euroclear, product and project leadership at Getinge, CTO at
      Northfork, interim Group CTO
      at Eniro Group, Head of Platform at Trustly, IT Director, North at Unilabs, CIO at MedHelp,
      and infrastructure leadership at Klarna. Earlier assignments include project and line
      management at Unibet.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before the leadership roles, the foundation was technical: systems, infrastructure and
      consulting from the late 1990s, then project and people leadership. A one-year systems
      engineering education sits at the start of that. Later training includes SAFe Product Owner /
      Product Manager, completed in 2024.
    </p>
    <p>
      The titles change. The work is to hold the technology agenda and stay close to delivery.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Still close to the work">
    <p>
      Advice that never meets a backlog, an incident or a user stays abstract. I still build and
      run My Star Day and Körpasset, alongside the consulting. A recommendation has to hold up
      against the architecture, the team, the release and the commercial side of a product.
    </p>
    <p>
      So the assignments are wider than a vacant CTO or CIO chair. Transformation, product
      direction, how an organisation delivers, and an AI ambition that has to become something
      someone can operate.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Career" title="Selected career experience">
    <Experience items={experience} detailed />
    <p class="note">
      Roles and years are taken from the previous public Papa Bravo site. Earlier systems and
      consulting work, before Unibet, is not listed organisation by organisation.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Papa Bravo">
    <p>
      Papa Bravo AB is the company. The work is consulting and advisory assignments, and the
      products the company builds and operates — My Star Day and Körpasset.
    </p>
    <p>
      Clients work with Pontus directly.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={site.linkedIn} rel="me noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
        Pontus Burman on LinkedIn
        <span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="working-together" eyebrow="Collaborators" title="Interested in working with Papa Bravo?">
    <p>
      Papa Bravo is not running a recruitment process, and there is no open role to apply for.
      There is a standing interest in meeting strong people in technology, product and design —
      for a future role, a consulting collaboration, or building products together.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Working%20with%20Papa%20Bravo`}>{site.email}</a>
    </p>
  </Section>

  <ContactCta />
</BaseLayout>
